{
  "Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Sign-In Events via Third-Party IdP",
  "Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Initial Access / T1199\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Sign-In Events via Third-Party IdP\" or \"<ip>|Okta Sign-In Events via Third-Party IdP\"\n\nFailed sign-ins through a third-party Identity Provider (user.authentication.auth_via_IDP, auth_via_inbound_SAML, auth_via_social, user.session.start) on the OAuth authorize callback, where Okta rejected the IdP's response: a replayed SAML assertion ID, an unresolvable IdP endpoint, an unmappable username, or a SAML response or assertion that failed validation. Replayed or forged assertions are how a compromised or spoofed IdP is abused.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_sign_in_events_via_third_party_idp/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/blob/main/rules/integrations/okta/initial_access_sign_in_events_via_third_party_idp.toml",
  "Labels": [
    "okta",
    "detection",
    "authentication-sessions",
    "initial-access",
    "T1199"
  ],
  "Schedule": "14,29,44,59 * * * *",
  "Duration": -900,
  "DefaultDeploymentRules": {
    "Disabled": false,
    "RunImmediately": false
  },
  "ScheduledType": "search",
